course: dictionary
lesson: 9256
title: Soup: a food and an idiom
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so look at the words around it. «One kind act, like bringing soup to someone ill, can end a feud.» Here soup is a food, because bringing it to someone who is ill is a caring thing to do.
explain: Soup is a hot liquid food made by cooking vegetables, meat, fish or other foods in water or stock. Words like hot, bowl and cooking are clues that the food meaning is the right one.
explain: In informal talk, «in the soup» means in trouble, and it is not about a bowl at all. Swap the meaning into the sentence to check: "He is in trouble now" makes sense, so the idiom fits.
fact: Soup is a noun, and its plural is soups.
fact: «Soup» means a hot liquid food made by cooking vegetables, meat, fish or other foods in water or stock.
fact: Tomato soup, chicken soup and vegetable soup are all kinds of soup, and you eat soup with a soup spoon.
fact: A soup kitchen gives free meals to people in need.
fact: «In the soup» (informal) means in trouble.
exercise: «One kind act, like bringing soup to someone ill, can end a feud.» What is the soup in this sentence? | A bowl with a lid | *A hot food brought to someone who is ill | A kind of bird | Trouble
exercise: A pot holds 12 litres of soup. Each bowl holds 2 litres. How many bowls can be filled? | *6 | 4 | 24 | 10
exercise: Ella says, «He is in the soup now after breaking the window.» What does in the soup mean? | Floating in a bowl | *In trouble | Happy and safe | Hungry for lunch
test: Which of these is a kind of soup? | Pencil | Soup spoon | *Vegetable soup | Soup kitchen
test: In the song «Beautiful Soup, so rich and green», what kind of song is it? | *A sad song | A football chant | A lullaby about the moon | A birthday song
exam: Which meaning fits «Dad found out, and now the whole family is in the soup»? | Full of vegetables | Hot and wet | Hungry | *In trouble
